{"archetypes":[{"name":"caller-census","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's shim-deletion ordering hinges on an exact caller count; a single missed larch_quiet_append_done_trap call site causes command-not-found under set -euo pipefail in production scripts","prompt_body":"Grep every `.sh` file in the repo for `larch_quiet_append_done_trap` and `larch_quiet_write_paired_pid_file` and compare the full hit list against the plan's enumerated scope (8 callers for the first, 0 `.sh` callers for the second). Pay particular attention to `run-step5-review.sh` and any dynamically sourced wrapper scripts that are not on the plan's file list. If any caller falls outside the plan's scope, the shim deletion will produce a `command not found` abort before the caller is cleaned up. Also verify that the plan's claimed line numbers for each call site (e.g., `ci-wait.sh:68`, `collect-agent-results.sh:308`) match the actual current file state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"xref-sweep","focus_area":"architecture","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan removes BASH_AUTHORING.md §4 and tombstones NEVER #16, but many docs reference these by name; stale pointers in out-of-scope files leave broken cross-references and may silently mislead future contributors","prompt_body":"Search all Markdown files, skill SKILL.md files, and `.claude/rules/*.md` files NOT on the plan's file list for the literal strings `BASH_AUTHORING.md §4`, `NEVER #16`, `lint-foreground-markers`, `lint-foreground`, `Family-B`, `Background pair required`, and `breadcrumb-monitor`. Any hit in an out-of-scope file is a plan gap that leaves stale cross-reference text pointing at deleted content or removed lint rules. Also check whether the AGENTS.md polling-loop bullet that currently ends with `see BASH_AUTHORING.md §4 and scripts/breadcrumb-monitor.md` will still resolve correctly after §4 deletion; the plan rewrites this bullet but the replacement text should not reference a now-deleted anchor. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"test-gap","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Three test harnesses are updated in the plan but the full test suite is broader; any harness outside the plan's file list that still asserts fence-shape presence or old sentinel exports will fail after Stage 4 collapses the fences","prompt_body":"Inspect every `scripts/test-*.sh` and `skills/*/scripts/test-*.sh` file NOT in the plan's file list for assertions involving `breadcrumb-monitor`, `Background pair required`, `LARCH_BREADCRUMB_STREAM`, `LARCH_DONE_SENTINEL`, `LARCH_STATUS_FILE`, or `LARCH_PAIRED_PID_FILE`. Check `scripts/test-implement-structure.sh` and `scripts/test-research-structure.sh` in particular, since those structure harnesses scan skill-fence shapes and may assert the old banner text. Also verify that after dropping `test-lib-quiet.sh` case 11 and renumbering 12-17 to 11-16, no other test file, `Makefile` target, or CI config references the old case numbers by ordinal. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
